          "label": "sonnet-baseline"
        },
        "response": {
          "output": "At two weeks in, you should be **prototyping the core loop to find out whether it's fun**. Don't build content or polish yet.\n\n**What to do now**\n1. Write a one-page concept: the core loop, the target experience, and the scope.\n2. Build the cheapest playable graybox of that loop.\n3. Playtest it with real players and watch where they struggle or get bored. Kill or rework the loop if it isn't fun.\n4. Keep a light, living GDD. Next comes a vertical slice, one piece built to shipping quality, before you scale up to full production.\n\n**Who you need**\n- **Design:** someone owning the core loop and GDD.\n- **Gameplay programming:** the prototype itself, plus the engine choice (Godot in this toolkit).\n- **Playtesting:** someone who runs sessions and reports what they saw.\n- **Later:** a producer for scope, then technical art, level and content, and audio. On a solo or indie project you cover most of these yourself.\n\nIs this solo or a team, and do you have a prototype yet? With that I can narrow this to your next two milestones."
        },
