        "prompt": {
          "raw": "You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\nThe game is feature-complete per the GDD. Are we ready to ship?",
          "label": "evals/game-development/prompt-baseline.txt: You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\n{{request}}",
          "config": {}
        },
        "promptId": "13f1d7f3102b636ca0ba6f9e94a02e6aab2a7355b61f0e6544b8303bd1294d94",
        "promptIdx": 0,
        "provider": {
          "id": "exec:../_provider/claude.sh",
          "label": "sonnet-baseline"
        },
        "response": {
          "output": "Not yet. Feature-complete per the GDD is alpha. It isn't ship-ready, because beta (content-complete) and gold still sit between you and release.\n\nCheck these before you call it done:\n\n- **Content-complete?** Are all levels, art, audio and text final, or are there still placeholders?\n- **Playtested?** Have people outside the team played the full game, not just the vertical slice? Do they find the fun and finish it?\n- **Last 10%:** Polish, bug triage and performance on target hardware. This usually takes about half the total time, so budget for it.\n- **Platform requirements:** Store page, build and rating for Steam or itch.io. Console cert if you're going there.\n- **Marketing:** Do you have a store page, wishlists, a trailer and a demo? If not, a launch now would get little visibility.\n- **Post-launch:** Is there a day-one patch plan, and someone to handle reviews and community?\n- **Monetization:** Does it avoid dark patterns such as loot boxes or manipulative FOMO?\n\nIf you tell me the target platform and what's left in the build, I can turn this into a go/no-go checklist for your project. I can also scan the repo for TODOs, placeholders and test status."
        },
